2. Can a Destructor be called explicitly in c++?

Yes, in c++ you can call explicitly call a destructor.

Eg:
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
class Demo{
public:
Demo(){cout<<"cnstr"<<endl;
~Demo(){cout<<"dstr"<<endl;}
};
int main()
{
Demo obj;
obj.~Demo();//Explicit dstr call;
cout<<"End prgm"<<endl;
}
